he built-in renderer, so you implement only the node types you want to change:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["struct MyDelegate: RichTextViewDelegate {","    typealias BlockLibrary = Content","","    @MainActor","    func view(for heading: RichText<Content>.Heading) -> any View {","        Text(heading.attributedString(baseFont: .title))","            .font(.system(.title, design: .serif))","    }","","    @MainActor","    func view(for codeBlock: RichText<Content>.CodeBlock) -> any View {","        MySyntaxHighlightedCode(codeBlock)","    }","}","","ScrollView { article.content }","    .richTextViewDelegate(MyDelegate())"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The delegate’s "},{"code":"BlockLibrary","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" associated type must match the rich text being rendered. The delegate applies to all rich text in the view hierarchy below the modifier; node types it does not implement keep their defaults."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"style":"note","name":"Note","type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Inline marks and unknown nodes have no delegate hook. Marks are rendered as part of their containing text run, and "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/RichTextView\/documentation\/RichTextView\/RichTextViewDelegate\/viewForHorizontalRule()","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" takes no node value because a horizontal rule carries no data."}]}]},{"level":2,"text":"Handling story links","anchor":"Handling-story-links","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Rich-text links that point at another Storyblok story are rendered with a "},{"code":"storyblok-story:\/\/<uuid>","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" URL rather than a web address. Use "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/RichTextView\/documentation\/RichTextView\/SwiftUICore\/View\/onStoryLink(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" to intercept taps on 